---
title: Step 5 against Step 6 - the same four requests, without and with invalidation (observed with curl)
---
sequenceDiagram
  actor Guest as Guests (curl)
  participant API as HTTP API
  participant Redis as Redis copy
  participant DB as Database (truth)

  rect rgb(255, 235, 238)
  Note over Guest,DB: Step 5 - python main.py --no-invalidation
  Guest->>API: 1. search 12-14 Nov
  API->>Redis: miss -> SET v0 "R7,R8" EX 30
  API-->>Guest: 200 R7, R8 (miss)
  Guest->>API: 2. Maya books R7
  API->>DB: has_overlap? no -> save R101, COMMIT
  API-->>Guest: 201 R101 (the copy is not touched)
  Guest->>API: 3. search again (within 30 s)
  API->>Redis: GET v0 -> "R7,R8"
  API-->>Guest: 200 R7, R8 (hit) - STALE: R7 is booked
  Guest->>API: 4. Omar asks for R7, 13-15 Nov
  API->>DB: has_overlap? yes (Maya)
  API-->>Guest: 409 Unavailable - the rule holds, nobody double-booked
  end

  rect rgb(232, 245, 233)
  Note over Guest,DB: Step 6 - python main.py (invalidation on)
  Guest->>API: 1. search 12-14 Nov
  API-->>Guest: 200 R7, R8 (miss, copy under v0)
  Guest->>API: 2. Maya books R7
  API->>DB: save R101, COMMIT
  API->>Redis: INCR availability:version -> 1
  API-->>Guest: 201 R101
  Guest->>API: 3. search again
  API->>Redis: GET v1:... -> nil (miss)
  API->>DB: has_overlap(R7)? yes, (R8)? no
  API-->>Guest: 200 R8 only (miss) - fresh
  Guest->>API: 4. Omar asks for R7
  API-->>Guest: 409 Unavailable
  end
